Note : I know you are seeing me use
getShieldedAddresses()
Let me explain why. It is the most convenient way to retrieve both keys in one call as it returns shieldedAddress, shieldedCoinPublicKey, and shieldedEncryptionPublicKey.
2. Statistics
The vault contract has a state called Balance
, it returns a set of Tokens Balances and what we did here was to iterate through balances array to find how many tokens with our token ID <-- For a token ID to appear you need to execute a mint operation.
